+
+Before calculations: supplied cubic compact Hamiltonian, dimensionless h(u)=aK+u sum_f(1-ReTr(U_f)/3), u=av, full physical or full link tensor space with vacuum constant. Rectangle C is planar R by S with R,S positive integers, normalized observable W_C=ReTr(U_C)/3. Prove vanishing Taylor coefficients below area RS from independent link-center charges of a Riesz-projection expression. Analytic continuation uses Tr(W P(u))/Tr(P(u)), never a conjugate-u normalized vector formula. Finite-volume analyticity alone is not an area law or volume-uniform complex bound.
+
+Prospective controls: oriented integral/mod3 face-boundary projection on a rectangle, repeated plaquette insertions cost multiplicity, no cancellation loophole from oppositely oriented charges, nonplanar faces cannot lower projected filling count. Independently check exposed root one-face candidate u/144. Attempt actual two-adjacent-face six-link loop leading coefficient via free resolvent energies and Haar contractions, not commuting scalar surrogate; no numeric candidate for this coefficient is assumed. Preserve failed routes and distinguish analytic all-order selection from existence/radius of an infinite-volume analytic expectation. No repo edits.
